26755a\",\"decision\":\"READY\",\"actions_or_findings\":[{\"title\":\"1. Implement official credential authentication and draft migration 0009\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\alembic\\\\versions\\\\20260919_0009_official_auth_identity_dispatch.py\",\"trigger\":\"Current authentication supports only Development and WeChat JWT methods; unknown WeChat identities silently create Users, while SMS, passwords, refresh, logout, and revocation are absent.\",\"rationale\":\"Create revision 20260919_0009 with down_revision=20260917_0007; do not modify 0001-0007, occupy 0008, or apply this draft to persistent databases. Add user_phones with unique user_id and phone_e164, user_passwords with unique user_id and Argon2id hash, sms_challenges with purpose/digest/expiry/attempt/consumed fields, auth_sessions with unique refresh-token digest/revocation/expiry/auth_method, and one-time wechat_link_challenges. OTPs must be random per challenge, HMAC-hashed with a server secret, TTL-bound, transactionally consumed once, retry-limited, and protected by atomic Redis phone/purpose and source rate limits; no fixed or master OTP and no OTP/password/token logging. Add an explicitly Development-only SMS provider that is injectable/capturable in tests but never returns the OTP from formal APIs; label all resulting evidence Fake/Development. Implement /auth/sms/send, /auth/sms/login, /auth/password/login, /auth/password/change, /auth/password/reset, /auth/token/refresh, /auth/logout, and authenticated phone/WeChat linking in backend/app/api/v1/auth.py, schema/auth.py, service/auth.py, repository/identity.py, provider/sms/__init__.py, provider/factory.py, core/security.py, core/config.py, and core/errors.py. Successful OTP login may create exactly one User only after phone proof and uniqueness locking; password login never creates one. Unknown WeChat openid must return a short-lived bind-required challenge without inserting User/UserWechat; after SMS/password proof it may bind to that same User, while an identity conflict returns merge-required and never auto-merges. JWTs accept auth_method sms|password|wechat plus development only in development/test, include a session identifier, and are rejected when the session is revoked; refresh tokens rotate and replay fails. Password reset/change revokes all old sessions and returns a new session according to policy. Preserve router-level DevAuth non-registration and verification rejection in staging/production. Replace the formal mini-program login flow in miniprogram/pages/login and services/auth.js/api.js with SMS/password tabs, refresh restoration, and optional WeChat linking; keep Seed buttons solely behind explicit LOCAL_PREVIEW in develop and never call /auth/dev/token from a formal action. Schema review must document that 0008 cannot later become a sibling of 0009: if outbox lands first, retarget 0009 to revise 0008; if 0009 lands first, 0008 must revise 0009. Operational rollback is disabling formal features/ai_auto_assign and forward-fixing; downgrade must abort if claimed employees or AUTO assignments make restoration of old NOT NULL constraints unsafe.\"},{\"title\":\"2. Add identity-neutral house catalog APIs and a formal resident picker\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\app\\\\api\\\\v1\\\\property_catalog.py\",\"trigger\":\"PropertyRepository already has hierarchy list methods, but no HTTP catalog routes exist and the mini-program requires a typed raw house_id.\",\"rationale\":\"Add authenticated GET /properties, /properties/{id}/buildings, /buildings/{id}/units, and /units/{id}/houses through new property catalog schemas/service plus api/v1/router.py. Each child query must derive and validate tenant/property ancestry from stored parent records, return only physical catalog fields, exclude resident relations, names, phones, bind requests, and ownership data, and reject cross-hierarchy or inactive-house traversal. Add a minimal authenticated profile update for display_name so the resident sequence is auth -> profile -> catalog. Rework miniprogram/pages/houses into cascading property/building/unit/room selectors; internal IDs may be submitted by selected controls but no formal text field may accept house_id. Continue using the existing POST /resident-bind-requests and manager approve/reject APIs unchanged. Tests must prove catalog responses contain no other resident data, parent-ID splicing fails, an unapproved applicant cannot read house-owned work orders or resident resources, and approval creates the existing ResidentHouseRelation rather than altering House.\"},{\"title\":\"3. Bind staff identities through controlled invites onto Employee\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\app\\\\service\\\\employee_identity.py\",\"trigger\":\"The current admin employee API requires an already-known user_id, and client-supplied identity data can therefore become the binding mechanism.\",\"rationale\":\"In 0009 make employees.user_id nullable while retaining its unique FK for claimed employees; existing non-null rows remain unchanged. Add employee_invites with employee/tenant composite FK, target phone, hashed random token, inviter, expiry, status, claimant, and consumed timestamp. The formal POST /admin/employees must create an unbound Employee plus EmployeeProperty/Duty/Skill data and an invite under employee:manage scope; keep direct user attachment only as an internal Development fixture helper. Add scoped resend/revoke endpoints and an authenticated claim endpoint that locks the invite and Employee, requires an ACTIVE Employee and a verified UserPhone equal to the invite target, rejects expiry/replay/conflict, and assigns employee.user_id exactly once. Resolve the STAFF role by Role.code and grant only scopes derived from current EmployeeProperty rows in the same transaction; never accept a role, user_id, tenant scope, property scope, or typed employee_no as authority. Add a small miniprogram employee-claim page accepting only the opaque invitation, with workbench visibility still derived from /me. Tests must cover a different authenticated User attempting the claim, employee_no-only attempts, disabled Employee, expired/replayed invite, duplicate Employee binding, cross-tenant manager, and permission revocation taking effect for an already-issued session.\"},{\"title\":\"4. Wire deterministic auto-assignment behind the disabled-by-default setting\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\app\\\\service\\\\auto_dispatch.py\",\"trigger\":\"AnalysisService currently writes hard-filtered, deterministically scored recommendations and always stops at PENDING_ASSIGNMENT; WorkOrderAssignment requires a human assigned_by_user_id.\",\"rationale\":\"Extend 0009 so existing work_order_assignments backfill assigned_source=HUMAN, assigned_by_user_id becomes nullable, a check enforces HUMAN => non-null and AUTO => null, and payload_json stores the analysis/recommendation/filter/score snapshot. Add provider_mode DEVELOPMENT|PRODUCTION to ai_call_logs and backfill existing rows DEVELOPMENT because the handoff identifies current evidence as Fake. When settings.ai_auto_assign is true, after successful validated analysis and recommendation creation, select the deterministic rank-1 eligible candidate without exposing employees to the LLM, lock the WorkOrder and EmployeeDailyStatus, re-run active User/STAFF role, Employee, EmployeeProperty, duty/skill, on-duty, and capacity checks, then atomically create the AUTO Assignment, increment load, update current_assignment_id, transition to ASSIGNED, and write SYSTEM WorkOrderLog/AuditLog records with actor_user_id null. Keep the setting False by default in persistent configuration. Low confidence, any non-none/high-risk result, provider failure/invalid output, no eligible candidate, disabled/revoked employee, or a concurrency conflict must retain the correct PENDING_ANALYSIS or PENDING_ASSIGNMENT human queue and record an explicit reason; these are fallbacks, not removal of auto-dispatch. Keep human assign/reassign intact with assigned_source=HUMAN. Do not create outbox/claim tables: future reserved 0008 owns reliable delivery claiming and must be linearly chained with 0009; auto-assignment's business transaction should expose a clean post-commit event boundary for that later migration.\"},{\"title\":\"5. Add negative-path tests and evidence gates without claiming live acceptance\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\tests\",\"trigger\":\"Historical VIS and Development-provider passes do not prove official authentication, real AI, or automatic Assignment creation.\",\"rationale\":\"Add focused unit and integration tests for wrong password; wrong, expired, retry-exhausted, and replayed OTP; SMS send limits; Argon2id storage; refresh replay and password-change/reset revocation; unknown-WeChat no-User side effect; unauthorized identity switching; unapproved house access; disabled Employee; live permission revocation with the same session; production DevAuth route and existing-token rejection; default-off auto-dispatch; enabled safe-result auto-dispatch creating WorkOrderAssignment without invoking the human assign endpoint; no-candidate/high-risk/low-confidence/provider-failure manual paths; concurrent assignment idempotency and capacity; and rejection of any LLM employee_id field. Provider-provenance tests must assert Development rows and reports cannot satisfy a real-AI gate, while PRODUCTION evidence requires provider_mode=PRODUCTION, configured model identity, validated structured output, downstream state, and no secret material��not merely adapter construction or HTTP 200. Cursor may write all tests now; this planning session ran none. Unit/static tests may run without external state, but DB-backed migration/runtime tests and 0009 upgrade/downgrade regression must wait for an explicitly authorized disposable database and must never target property_ai, property_ai_day4, or recreate/wipe shared mysql-test. Produce separate softwa